Why Is Demand Increasing
Semiconductor Miniaturization: Smaller nodes and increasingly complex 3D architectures require highly precise measurement of internal structures and material layers.
Advanced Packaging: Hybrid bonding, complex system-in-package designs, and other advanced packaging technologies are increasing demand for non-destructive inspection and metrology.
Automated Quality Control: AI-enabled analysis and automated measurement are helping manufacturers improve throughput, defect detection, and process-control capabilities.

X-Ray Metrology System Watch: Inline and Hybrid Metrology
The industry is moving toward faster, automated, and integrated X-ray metrology platforms. Inline and at-line systems can provide process-control data directly within manufacturing environments, while hybrid platforms combining X-ray with other measurement technologies can deliver broader inspection capabilities for advanced semiconductor and industrial applications.

